      "text": "The \"love hut\" tradition has largely declined or disappeared among the Kreung. It was practiced only in the far northeast of Cambodia, particularly in Ratanakiri, among certain indigenous groups. It is better understood as a traditional practice with strong cultural links to the indigenous peoples of the Laos–Cambodia border region, rather than as a Khmer tradition. In fact, it belongs more to the past than to present-day Cambodian culture and has nothing to do with mainstream Khmer culture.\nThis video is total AI-crap!",
